WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.340
so let's practice calculating
equilibrium concentrations

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:17.160
consider the following equilibrium with
N2 + 3H2 in equilibrium with 2NH3

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:24.449
now at equilibrium the nitrogen
concentration is 4 point 2 6 molar the

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:29.970
hydrogen concentration is 2 point zero 9
molar and the equilibrium constant for

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:36.030
this system is zero point zero six zero
zero what is the equilibrium

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:42.050
concentration of NH3? so if this seems
confusing check out my tutorial on

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.400
equilibria and then give this a try.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.400
so this is a very straightforward situation

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.630
here is our equilibrium now the first
thing we want to do is generate our

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:15.000
equilibrium constant expression now
recall that will involve placing the

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.159
concentrations of the products over the
concentrations of the reactants and then

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:24.530
the concentrations are going to be
raised to the power of the relevant

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:29.610
stoichiometric coefficient so whatever
the coefficient is on a substance the

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:35.159
concentration of that substance will be
raised to that power so in this case we

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:40.229
have our equilibrium constant being
equal to the concentration of ammonia

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:44.939
squared because ammonia has a
coefficient of 2 over the concentration

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:50.310
of nitrogen times the concentration of
hydrogen raised to the 3rd power because

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:56.939
hydrogen has a coefficient of 3 so that
is our expression and now we just plug

00:01:56.939 --> 00:02:01.979
in what we know and as it turns out we
know everything except one thing so we

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:07.079
have that constant it is zero point zero
six zero zero we have our nitrogen

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:11.190
concentration it's four point two six
and we have our hydrogen concentration

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.359
it's two point zero nine
and that will be raised to the third

00:02:15.359 --> 00:02:20.219
power so here all we have to do is a
little bit of arithmetic and we get the

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:25.230
ammonia concentration squared as being
equal to two point three three and then

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:31.159
we take the square root and our answer
will be one point five three molar.

